From 29b70536ccd25cb27b984b8cf11ae622648b4ff2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 0xFFshell <>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 09:25:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] elytra: do not ask a player who is not there on the way out
 of a world

The teardown ask added for a begun auto-swap read ctx.player().containerMenu in
ElytraBehavior#finishTheSwapBeforeGoing. The way out of a world reaches
ElytraProcess#onLostControl with no player: the first tick without one runs
PathingControlManager#cancelEverything, and ElytraProcess#onWorldEvent destroys
the behaviour only on the way into a world (its test is getWorld() != null, not
the exit the comment said). With the process holding a live behaviour, Save and
Quit to Title - or a disconnect - threw a NullPointerException from the tick and
the game crashed. The headless client reproduced it: #elytra, then Save and Quit.

The helper now looks for the player first; with none there is no window and
nothing to send a click to, and the queue goes with the behaviour. The comments
and HUMANLIKE.md that carried the wrong premise are corrected, and a pin in
InventoryTransactionTest fails with the original unguarded body and with a body
that touches the player before it looks. The in-game check is scripts/headless/
smoke.sh, which exited 1 on the crash and 0 here.
---
 HUMANLIKE.md                                  |  5 +-
 .../java/baritone/process/ElytraProcess.java  |  4 +-
 .../process/elytra/ElytraBehavior.java        | 14 +++--
 .../utils/InventoryTransactionTest.java       | 52 +++++++++++++++++--
 4 files changed, 64 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/HUMANLIKE.md b/HUMANLIKE.md
index f8f1d65b..30e8b826 100644
--- a/HUMANLIKE.md
+++ b/HUMANLIKE.md
@@ -89,8 +89,9 @@ worn one still on the back, arrived at by a different road than the window going
 finishes a sequence that has begun (`InventoryTransaction#finishNow`, asked from
 `ElytraProcess#onLostControl`), spends its remaining gaps doing it, and gives up whole one that has not -
 nothing happened, so the job asks again. The ask sits in `onLostControl` and not in `destroyBehaviorAsync`
-on purpose: that runs on the executor, where a window click has no client thread to be sent on, and
-`onWorldEvent` reaches it on the way out of a world, where there is nothing left to send it to. A begun
+on purpose: that runs on the executor, where a window click has no client thread to be sent on. The way out
+of a world reaches `onLostControl` too, from the first tick with no player, so the ask looks for the player
+first: with none there is no window and nothing to send a click to, and the queue goes with the behaviour. A begun
 sequence whose window is *not* the player's own is left exactly as it was rather than fired into a menu that
 would drop it, because clearing a queue that never ran turns "stalled and still retryable" into "stalled and
 silently abandoned".
diff --git a/src/main/java/baritone/process/ElytraProcess.java b/src/main/java/baritone/process/ElytraProcess.java
index a354d7ef..3f28a5a2 100644
--- a/src/main/java/baritone/process/ElytraProcess.java
+++ b/src/main/java/baritone/process/ElytraProcess.java
@@ -102,8 +102,8 @@ public class ElytraProcess extends BaritoneProcessHelper implements IBaritonePro
         this.goal = null;
         // A swap that has begun is finished rather than dropped: letting go of the behaviour stops the
         // drain that runs its clicks, and the half-applied state is the one the window rule exists to
-        // avoid. Asked here rather than in destroyBehaviorAsync, which runs on the executor and is also
-        // reached on the way out of a world. See InventoryTransaction#finishNow.
+        // avoid. Asked here rather than in destroyBehaviorAsync, which runs on the executor. The way out of
+        // a world reaches this too, with no player to ask: see ElytraBehavior#finishTheSwapBeforeGoing.
         if (this.behavior != null) {
             this.behavior.finishTheSwapBeforeGoing();
         }
diff --git a/src/main/java/baritone/process/elytra/ElytraBehavior.java b/src/main/java/baritone/process/elytra/ElytraBehavior.java
index ca5503ee..59d3c440 100644
--- a/src/main/java/baritone/process/elytra/ElytraBehavior.java
+++ b/src/main/java/baritone/process/elytra/ElytraBehavior.java
@@ -1333,11 +1333,19 @@ public final class ElytraBehavior implements Helper {
      * being asked the moment {@code ElytraProcess} drops its reference - see {@link InventoryTransaction#finishNow}.
      * <p>
      * Called from {@code ElytraProcess#onLostControl}, which is client-thread like every other caller of it,
-     * and deliberately not from {@code destroyBehaviorAsync}: that runs on the executor, and it is also
-     * reached on the way out of a world, where a window click has nothing to be sent to.
+     * and deliberately not from {@code destroyBehaviorAsync}, which runs on the executor.
+     * <p>
+     * The way out of a world reaches {@code onLostControl} too, and with no player: the first tick without
+     * one runs {@code PathingControlManager#cancelEverything}, and {@code ElytraProcess#onWorldEvent}
+     * destroys the behaviour only on the way <em>into</em> a world (its test is {@code getWorld() != null}).
+     * Then there is no window to click in and nothing to send a click to, and the queue goes with the
+     * behaviour: reading the player there was a NullPointerException from the tick, a crash on Save and
+     * Quit with the elytra process active.
      */
     public void finishTheSwapBeforeGoing() {
-        invTransaction.finishNow(ctx.player().containerMenu == ctx.player().inventoryMenu);
+        if (ctx.player() != null) {
+            invTransaction.finishNow(ctx.player().containerMenu == ctx.player().inventoryMenu);
+        }
     }
 
     private void queueWindowClick(int windowId, int slotId, int button, ContainerInput type) {
diff --git a/src/test/java/baritone/utils/InventoryTransactionTest.java b/src/test/java/baritone/utils/InventoryTransactionTest.java
index 6c881c69..1f5d7bcc 100644
--- a/src/test/java/baritone/utils/InventoryTransactionTest.java
+++ b/src/test/java/baritone/utils/InventoryTransactionTest.java
@@ -259,9 +259,9 @@ public class InventoryTransactionTest {
      * <p>
      * Two things have to hold and both are about <em>where</em> the ask sits. It has to be in
